meta {
  name: current user
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/rest-auth/user/
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessTokenStudent}}
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  dj-rest-auth's own "who am I". Returns the `User` row only -- no `role`, and no
  Admin/Teacher/Student profile.

  For anything role-aware prefer the payload from **login**, or
  `GET /student/me/` for a student's own profile. This is kept because
  dj-rest-auth routes it and some clients expect it.

  `PUT` / `PATCH` on the same URL edit `first_name`, `last_name` and `username`.
  They do **not** touch the Student profile -- name, country, timezone and level
  live on `PATCH /student/me/`.

  ## API example response
  {
    "pk": 4,
    "username": "marco.reyes@example.com",
    "email": "marco.reyes@example.com",
    "first_name": "Marco",
    "last_name": "Reyes"
  }
}
